"""Question-design review for personal and home security education."""
from review_angle_plans import revise_domain, audit

PERSONAL = """history_origins|How a Safety Practice Developed|Which documented risk led to one personal-safety practice?|Use dated public guidance and evaluation records.
famous_examples|A Safety Campaign Reexamined|Did a well-known campaign reduce its target harm?|Compare design, reach, outcome, and alternative explanations.
hidden_stories|Safety Burdens Unequally Shared|Whose safety needs are missing from common advice?|Use disaggregated risk and access evidence.
beginner_explainers|Understanding Risk in Context|How can a person assess a stated risk without panic?|Explain exposure, likelihood, severity, and reliable sources.
advanced_concepts|Security and Freedom Tradeoffs|When can a protective measure create a new privacy or access burden?|Compare evaluated outcomes for defined groups.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Safety Trend With Unclear Cause|Which factors may explain a change in reported personal harm?|Account for reporting and exposure differences.
technology_innovation|A Personal-Safety Tool Evaluated|Did one alert tool improve response without false reassurance?|Compare reliability, accessibility, privacy, and measured outcomes.
people_personalities|Who Designed the Guidance?|Whose input shaped one safety campaign?|Use committee records and affected-community feedback.
major_events|A Safety Rule After an Incident|What changed after one documented personal-safety event?|Compare inquiry findings, adopted policy, and later evidence.
how_it_works|A Help-Seeking Pathway|What happens after a person requests help from a public service?|Map official contact, triage, referral, and support at a high level.
rise_fall|A Safety Program's Capacity|Why did one support program expand or contract?|Compare funding, staffing, demand, and outcomes.
then_vs_now|Personal Safety Across Two Periods|Did risk change for the same defined population?|Use comparable definitions, survey methods, and exposure.
future_developments|A Conditional Safety Proposal|Which condition would determine whether a new service helps?|State target group, accessibility, resources, and evaluation.
myths_vs_facts|Testing a Common Safety Claim|Does a popular warning match measured risk?|Check denominators, setting, and reporting limitations.
documentary_stories|One Person's Safety Experience|What can a consented account show about accessing help?|Protect identity and avoid treating one experience as universal.
incident_timeline|A Public Safety Incident's Record|Which sequence is supported by released documents?|Avoid identifying details and label uncertain timing.
prevention_layer|Prevention Without Blame|Which evaluated community or environmental measure reduced harm?|Avoid implying a victim caused the event.
response_chain|From Alert to Support|Where does responsibility pass between a service and support provider?|Use public process descriptions and consented accounts.
evidence_integrity|Reading Risk Statistics|How do reporting rates affect a personal-safety statistic?|Compare survey, administrative, and incident data.
victim_perspective|Choice After Harm|Which services and decisions mattered to an affected person?|Center consent, autonomy, and privacy.
system_failure|A Documented Service Gap|Which institutional barrier prevented timely help?|Use official inquiry findings, not speculative blame.
risk_communication|A Warning People Can Use|Did a public notice explain a risk and safe next step clearly?|Assess timing, language, disability access, and feedback.
community_trust|Trusted Routes to Help|Why might a defined community hesitate to contact a service?|Use attributed accounts and service design evidence.
false_positive|The Cost of a False Alert|What happened when one safety signal was inaccurate?|Use documented outcomes and avoid revealing exploitable mechanisms.
after_action|A Recommendation Followed Up|Was one inquiry recommendation funded and implemented?|Compare report, policy, and later evaluation.
legal_boundary|Rights When Seeking Help|Which privacy or reporting rule applies to one service?|Specify jurisdiction and date; do not offer case-specific legal advice.
resilience_design|Support During Disruption|Which public-facing help channel remained accessible during an outage?|Use continuity plans and measured availability.
field_evidence_handling|A Safe Record of a Report|What information can a public service document without exposing a person?|Use privacy policy and consent standards.
field_prevention_design|A Safety Intervention Tested|Did one prevention design reduce a defined harm?|Compare exposed groups and evaluation methods.
field_response_timing|When Help Arrived|Which stage of a service pathway accounts for delay?|Use public metrics and avoid operational vulnerabilities.
field_public_trust|Explaining a Service Failure|How did an agency account for a contested response?|Compare released findings and affected voices.
field_victim_support|Support Beyond Immediate Danger|What assistance was available afterward?|Use current official service rules and consented testimony."""

HOME = """history_origins|How a Home-Safety Standard Emerged|Which documented home hazard led to a standard?|Use dated code, incident, and evaluation records.
famous_examples|A Home-Security Product Under Review|What does one widely promoted system actually detect and miss?|Compare contract, test conditions, and independent evidence.
hidden_stories|Who Bears Home-Security Costs?|Which residents lack control over locks, devices, or building repairs?|Use tenure, disability, and income evidence.
beginner_explainers|Layers of Home Security|Which functions do physical barriers, alerts, and response each serve?|Explain at a high level without bypass instructions.
advanced_concepts|Reliability Versus False Alarms|How do false alerts and missed events affect a system's usefulness?|Compare independent tests and real-use data.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Home Alarm With an Unclear Outcome|Which records can establish what one alarm did?|Separate device logs, response records, and unknowns.
technology_innovation|A Connected Home Device Tested|Did one device improve safety while protecting privacy?|Compare reliability, updates, data handling, and accessibility.
people_personalities|Who Set Building Security Rules?|Which owner, regulator, or resident decision changed protection?|Trace public records and affected voices.
major_events|A Building Incident and Rule Change|Which home-safety requirement followed a documented incident?|Compare recommendation, adoption, enforcement, and outcomes.
how_it_works|From Sensor to Alert|What happens when a home device reports an event?|Map device, network, monitoring, notification, and response at a safe level.
rise_fall|A Security Service That Failed|Why did one monitoring service lose reliability or coverage?|Use public outages, maintenance, and contract records.
then_vs_now|Home Protection Across Two Periods|How did one housing type's safety provisions change?|Compare code, adoption, costs, and accessibility.
future_developments|A Conditional Smart-Home Proposal|Which safeguards would a new device need before adoption?|State privacy, reliability, accessibility, and support criteria.
myths_vs_facts|Testing a Home-Security Promise|Does a product claim match its disclosed limits?|Check independent evaluation and contract exclusions.
documentary_stories|One Household's Safety Upgrade|What did a documented upgrade change and leave unresolved?|Use consented accounts and applicable building records.
incident_timeline|A Home-Safety Event in Records|What do released incident and service logs establish?|Protect occupants and avoid exploitable details.
prevention_layer|A Building-Level Prevention Measure|Did a code or maintenance change reduce a defined home risk?|Use evaluated measures for comparable buildings.
response_chain|When a Home Alert Reaches Help|Who receives and acts on one type of alarm?|Read provider and public-service terms, not assumed response.
evidence_integrity|What Device Logs Can Prove|How reliable are logs for reconstructing a home event?|Inspect clock, retention, gaps, and privacy controls.
victim_perspective|Residents After a Home Incident|What needs did consenting residents identify after a breach or hazard?|Center privacy, housing stability, and support.
system_failure|A Documented Building Safeguard Gap|Which maintenance or governance failure was established?|Use official inquiry and avoid tactical detail.
risk_communication|An Alert Residents Understand|Could residents act on one warning, including those with disabilities?|Assess format, timing, language, and false alarms.
community_trust|Shared-Building Security|How do residents evaluate a building's safety process?|Use tenant accounts and transparent service records.
false_positive|When an Alarm Was Wrong|What costs did one false alert impose on residents and responders?|Use public data and product terms.
after_action|Was a Home-Safety Fix Implemented?|Which recommendation was actually completed after an incident?|Compare inquiry, inspection, and later evidence.
legal_boundary|Consent and Home Monitoring|Who may install or access one monitoring system?|Specify tenure, jurisdiction, privacy rule, and date.
resilience_design|Safety During Power or Network Loss|Which public-level backup preserved an alert function?|Use product tests and maintenance records without bypass details.
field_evidence_handling|Privacy in Home-Security Records|Who can access, retain, or share device recordings?|Read provider policy and applicable law.
field_prevention_design|A Safer Building Feature|Did one physical design change reduce a measured home hazard?|Compare comparable buildings and maintenance quality.
field_response_timing|Alarm-to-Action Interval|Which stages account for delay after a home alert?|Use public service data and avoid exposing vulnerabilities.
field_public_trust|Transparency After a Security Failure|What did a provider or landlord disclose after a failure?|Compare notices, remediation, and resident feedback.
field_victim_support|Help After a Home Incident|Which housing, repair, or victim services were available?|Use official eligibility and consented accounts."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("493", "493_personal_security", PERSONAL,
                  "Evidence-based personal safety, help pathways, privacy, accessibility, and support after harm.",
                  "dated public guidance, program evaluations, incident data methods, privacy rules, and consented accounts",
                  "Do not blame victims or provide tactical instructions; specify jurisdiction and current local guidance.")
    revise_domain("494", "494_home_security", HOME,
                  "Home and building security through product limits, resident rights, alerts, privacy, maintenance, and support.",
                  "dated product terms, independent tests, building codes, incident reviews, and consented resident accounts",
                  "Avoid bypass details; verify current product terms, local law, privacy, and housing tenure.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
